# The runtime's memory functions: memcpy, memmove, memset, and memcmp, which compiled code
# and LLVM call, and the byte comparisons compiled code asks the runtime for
# (refined_bytes_equal, refined_find). memcpy and memset move eight bytes at a time; none of
# them calls another C function, since they are what such calls would reach.
#
# This module is generated from tools/memory.dsl by tools/build.py.

